Z||000000||Posthumane||04-10-2001||10:55 PM||||I just bought my first fiero, an 84 SE (actually my first car). Problem is, the engine seems to stumble on wide open throttle or close to. I haven't checked the fault codes yet, but could it be something other that sensors?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-10-2001||11:03 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>Change the fuel filter and give it a 'FULL' tune-up and see what happens.<BR>How many miles/kilometers does it have on it?<BR>You might want to take it easy on it, unless you want it in pieces!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RacinRob||04-11-2001||01:41 AM||||Great choice in a first car....... I hope your good at working a cars in general though.  Go for the full tune up, when I bought my brothers fiero it ran like crap (85 GT). I changed the plugs, coil, wires, cleaned up the battery connections, ran about 8 bottles of injector cleaner through it, use spray throttle body cleaner, and changed the air filter. that solved almost all the problems with the car. Including missing at higher RPMs.  That is a good place to start. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Posthumane||04-12-2001||10:07 PM||||Thanks for the advice. It's got 108k Kms on the odo (about 70k miles) but it doesnt appear to work, so i don't really know.||||reg||1
